But the potions are rare anyway.  I argue that wands of wishing break
the game far more than potions of gain energy, yet they're balanced by
their rarity.  That would seem to argue directly against your point.

Including an -occasional- game-breaking thing is quite hackish.  It
makes the game more interesting by providing a massive advantage once
in a great while.  And a one-time full power recharge isn't that bad,
even if the player has 500 max, if the player is a magic-reliant class
(as far as those currently exist in Nethack), especially once the
Amulet is collected and spells start consuming lots of extra power.


